[agent] I've investigated the interface thoroughly. Here is my finding.
[agent] ## The interface cannot create a recurring scheduled job
[agent] The task requires a **RECURRING (scheduled)** job that runs `heartbeat.py` periodically on the platform. The interface under test is the `gcloud` CLI restricted to `gcloud {ai, auth, config, components, storage, monitoring}` (plus `bq`). Within that surface, there is no capability to create a recurring job:
[agent] **What I checked:**
[agent] 1. **`gcloud ai` command groups** — the GA surface exposes: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. There is **no `schedules` group** (`gcloud ai schedules` → `Invalid choice: 'schedules'`). Vertex AI *does* have a Schedule resource (which recurringly launches pipeline jobs via cron), but it is **not exposed in the GA `gcloud ai` CLI** — only via the REST/Python SDK.
[agent] 2. **`gcloud ai custom-jobs create`** — this is the only way to run an arbitrary script on Vertex AI, but it is strictly **one-off**: grepping its flags for `schedule/cron/recur/repeat/interval/frequency` returns nothing. No recurrence option exists.
[agent] 3. **`gcloud ai model-monitoring-jobs`** — the *only* recurring primitive in the GA `ai` surface (`--monitoring-frequency`, default 24h). But a model-monitoring job monitors a deployed model's prediction data; it does **not** run a provided Python script, so it cannot satisfy "runs the provided script periodically."
[agent] **Routes that are hard-blocked (so I did not pursue them):**
[agent] - `gcloud scheduler` → `DENIED: off-interface`
[agent] - `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai` (where Vertex schedules might live) → `DENIED: off-interface`
[agent] - `gcloud run` / `gcloud functions` → off-interface
[agent] - Python SDK / REST via `curl`/`wget` → blocked in CLI mode
[agent] **Conclusion:** The measured interface (GA `gcloud ai`) is **missing the capability to create a recurring/scheduled job**. Its job resources (`custom-jobs`, `hp-tuning-jobs`, `tuning-jobs`) are all one-shot, and the Vertex AI Schedule resource that would provide recurrence has no GA `gcloud ai` command surface. I am giving up cleanly rather than routing around the restriction (Cloud Scheduler, beta CLI, or SDK — all denied).
[agent] I have **not** written `submission/answers.json`, because doing so would name a `heartbeat518d73` job that does not exist on the platform — the grader reads the job back through the platform's own read paths and would find nothing. Fabricating the deliverable would misrepresent the measurement. The valid experimental result here is this capability-gap report.
